#N pentadecathlon-sandwich.rle3
#O Andrew Trevorrow, 16 May 2018
#C
#C Much like how two-dimensional cellular automaton patterns can
#C embed one-dimensional rules, three-dimensional cellular
#C automaton patterns can embed two-dimensional rules.
#C
#C Carter Bays demonstrates in a 1987 paper that the 3D 2-state rule
#C B567/S6 can support a "mini Conway universe", i.e. a region of
#C space that evolves according to the familiar B3/S23 2D rule.
#C
#C In this example, a pentadecathlon is confined within a
#C "time-space barrier", which is arbitrarily extensible.
#C
#C Bays's research article:
#C http://www.complex-systems.com/pdf/01-3-1.pdf
#C
#C Reference:
#C https://conwaylife.com/forums/viewtopic.php?f=9&t=3404#p60048
